A||N||2||Lewis||Cleaning throttle body||||5||
Z||000000||Lewis||05-31-2000||10:08 PM||||I removed the plastic tube to my throttle body and stuck my finger in it and found a lot of black soot and greasy grime.  I know it has to be cleaned.  Can I open up the flap that is inside and spray in it or do I have to keep it closed?  Also how do I remove the IAC to clean it?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Ed||06-01-2000||01:38 AM||||You can spray carb cleaner into the V-6 throttle body while the engine is running.  Open the "air flap" and spray into the body. The engine may stall or act like it doesn't like the spray, but nothing bad will happen.   <P>WATCH OUT THAT THE LITTLE TUBE DOESN'T FLY OFF THE SPRAY CAN AND GO INTO YOUR MANIFOLD!  <BR>Sorry about the emphasis, but it happened to me but I was able to retrieve it.  Another owner wasn't so lucky: the tube did go into his manifold.  I heard that it melted there with no ill effect!  <P>The IAC can be screwed off but I haven't personally done it so no good suggestions except I've heard that you should be careful because it is plastic and can break.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||06-01-2000||03:04 AM||||I was lucky enough to have the plenum off yesterday to change the egr tube gasket to it and while I had it off as well as the plastic tube I got to quite liberal with throttle body cleaner at BOTH ends of it and 3 shop rags later you could've eaten off it! Well, it's very clean anyways  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 06-01-2000).]||||reg||1
